        "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{2}).$",
        "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{5!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{2} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
